1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
= www.kisskh.asia =

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

3
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:38,760
ADAPTED FROM THE ORIGINAL WEB NOVEL
THE EARLY SPRING, BY GU NIANG BIE KU

4
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,920
What would you have said?

5
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,960
And back then, I was craving
my dad's braised fish.

6
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,080
Do not halt the project.

7
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,120
Make sure everything is in order.

8
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,440
I'll rush back now.

9
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:20,640
Dad.

10
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,360
I feel cold.

11
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:24,880
I have work to do.

12
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,080
Your mom will be here later.

13
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,440
Call the nurse if you need anything.

14
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:18,200
FOLLOW ME HOME

15
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,880
You didn't have to come to work this soon.

16
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,280
Running around won't do
your recovery any good.

17
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:43,520
Your arm hasn't healed yet,
and you are driving.

18
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:48,240
I use my hands to steer, not my arms.

19
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,160
Shang Zhitao.

20
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:57,120
At work, courtesy is redundant.

21
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,120
It's all about an air of gravitas.

22
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,040
If your opponent knows you're a pushover,

23
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,360
you'll be swallowed whole.

24
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,480
Noted. Thank you.

25
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:09,920
Didn't I tell you to stop
thanking someone easily?

26
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,960
Have you forgotten?

27
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,800
I'll bear that in mind, Luke.

28
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:23,640
Are you not going to ask
where we are going?

29
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,280
Aren't you afraid I'll sell you out?

30
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,080
I owe my life to you.

31
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:32,080
Whatever it is, it's my treat.

32
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:36,120
I owe my life to you too.

33
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:38,080
How do you want me to repay it?

34
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:45,520
I hate owing someone a favor.

35
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,600
Let's just pretend
it's just you who owes me a favor.

36
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:55,440
Then, how do you want me to repay you?

37
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,480
Slowly.

38
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:54,520
This… This is a restaurant?

39
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,360
Are you afraid I'll dump your body
in the wilderness?

40
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:04,440
BE BACK SOON

41
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:05,480
Mian is waiting for you.

42
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:09,720
Let's go in.

43
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,320
Okay.

44
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:28,400
BE BACK SOON

45
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,440
Over here.

46
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,680
Careful.

47
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:23,080
Thanks.

48
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,000
Didn't you say
you were craving braised fish?

49
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,480
Which one do you want? Catch it yourself.

50
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:44,720
You must be the smart student
who doesn't need to study hard

51
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:46,800
to get first place in your examinations.

52
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:49,400
Do you truly think
smart students never study?

53
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:53,240
I used to think hard work would pay off,

54
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:56,520
but I don't think so anymore.

55
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,800
How's the catch?

56
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,160
Did you get any fish?

57
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,240
Tan Mian.

58
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:09,120
Owner of this private restaurant.

59
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,000
Also an advertisement veteran
who knows how to cook the best.

60
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,560
Thank you.

61
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,560
Shang Zhitao.

62
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:18,000
- Hi, Ms. Shang.
- Hi.

63
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,640
All right. Stop fishing. It's tedious.

64
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,560
Ms. Shang. Which one do you want?

65
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,160
I brought a net to scoop it up for you.

66
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:31,960
Teaching one to fish
is better than giving them a fish.

67
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:35,920
Yes. I want to catch one myself.

68
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,680
Luke, thanks for teaching me how to fish.

69
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,920
I now understand that
not only do I have to work hard,

70
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,520
but I have to seize the right timing too.

71
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,000
I didn't teach you anything.

72
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,280
You learned it yourself.

73
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,720
The food is ready.

74
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:07,320
Try it.

75
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:10,560
My secret grilled fish.

76
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,360
Thank you.

77
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:26,800
Girlfriend?

78
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:28,720
No.

79
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,720
Luke and I are colleagues.

80
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,600
Does she look like my girlfriend at all?

81
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,400
Right.

82
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:43,520
Then, this colleague of yours
must be more important than a girlfriend.

83
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:46,960
You are serving her personally.

84
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:50,280
Focus when you're eating fish.

85
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,280
Enjoy it.

86
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,400
- It's nice.
- Right?

87
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,320
The fish you caught
will always taste good.

88
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,040
If you know how to use bait,

89
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,680
you won't find yourself lacking in fish.

90
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:13,560
Yes. We should always learn from Luke

91
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:15,120
so that we don't become idiots.

92
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,240
You hold grudges.

93
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,240
Ms. Shang.

94
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,440
I have a question.

95
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:29,240
What do you think
is Luke's biggest talent?

96
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:32,760
His creativity.

97
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,800
Everyone says Luke

98
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:37,120
is a prodigy in the advertising industry
that you can't find elsewhere.

99
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:39,880
Prodigy?

100
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,760
Ten years ago, I thought so too.

101
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:46,240
I thought one good slogan
could leverage the entire Pacific Ocean.

102
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,080
But you can generate
as much hype as you want.

103
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:49,840
If your client's products
are not sold out,

104
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:53,200
they won't give you the budget
to support your vision.

105
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,360
See, Ms. Shang?

106
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:01,080
His biggest talent is not creativity,

107
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,040
but nitpicking.

108
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:06,000
When he nitpicks,

109
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:09,040
his words are more precise than a slogan.

110
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,400
Dig in.

111
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,600
It's probably a circuit breaker trip.

112
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,160
Just eat. Let me check on it.

113
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:34,600
How did you come in?

114
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:35,600
You pried the lock open?

115
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,600
Mr. Tan.

116
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:39,840
Where is Luan Nian?

117
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:41,960
Luan Nian?

118
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:43,080
I told you he and I are no longer friends.

119
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:45,000
We have closed. Just leave.

120
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,200
How many drinks did you have?

121
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:50,640
- I'll hail a taxi to get you home.
- I heard someone talking inside.

122
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,680
- Hey you…
- You're lying to me!

123
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:52,560
Why would I lie to you?

124
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,120
Luan Nian is inside. I know it.

125
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,280
- Luan Nian!
- No, he isn't.

126
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:57,280
- It's my other friend.
- Listen. You're there, aren't you?

127
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,680
Luan Nian isn't here.

128
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:00,560
If you lie to me,
I'll burn your restaurant.

129
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,120
Burn my restaurant?

130
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,720
That's a crime, miss.

131
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,720
Do you know
how much jail time you will get?

132
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,520
Stop taking me for a fool.

133
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:10,200
- Luan Nian! I know you're in there.
- He isn't here.

134
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:12,480
- Don't ignore me. Come out.
- Just leave.

135
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,520
- Luan Nian! Luan Nian!
- Go.

136
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:15,680
- Careful.
- He isn't here.

137
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:16,640
Just go.

138
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,760
- Luan Nian!
- Careful.

139
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,920
- Don't worry.
- Don't ignore me.

140
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:19,920
Come out now!

141
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,120
Just let me see you. We need to talk.

142
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,200
Luan Nian!

143
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,280
- I won't leave unless you come out.
- What happened?

144
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,560
- Luan Nian!
- Something came up.

145
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:29,840
Let's call it a day now.

146
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:31,600
- Luan Nian.
- After she leaves,

147
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:32,800
I'll drive you back.

148
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:34,160
Okay.

149
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,360
Luan Nian.

150
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,080
I finally get to see you.

151
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,480
Luan Nian.

152
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,720
I'm begging you.

153
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,400
Let's get back together.

154
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,480
I won't be what I was before.

155
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:06,840
I'll change.

156
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:09,880
Zhang Xin.

157
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,160
We already broke up.

158
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,040
You need to accept the truth.

159
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:17,600
There's no point in holding
onto this any longer.

160
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,320
No point?

161
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:26,240
For you, I argued with my parents,

162
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:29,800
gave up everything I had in the US,
and returned to Beijing.

163
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:33,600
- Is that nothing in your eyes?
- You made the decision yourself.

164
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,800
Don't pin that on me.

165
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:39,200
We both chose to break up.

166
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:40,640
It's been a year.

167
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,880
You've been texting, calling,
and stalking me.

168
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,320
Enough is enough.

169
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,480
It's time to put an end to this.

170
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,680
I am having a private moment
with my friend.

171
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,040
Please leave.

172
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,320
Your friend?

173
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,240
Don't deny it.

174
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:58,400
She's your new love interest.

175
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,840
Relationships go through ups and downs.

176
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:10,200
We broke up.

177
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:13,000
So, I'll just wait
until you break up with her.

178
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:16,960
When did you two get together?

179
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:22,000
You misunderstood.

180
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,920
We're just co-workers.

181
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,080
This is between us.

182
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:27,960
Do not involve other people.

183
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,320
Go inside first.

184
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:36,040
- Don't come near me!
- Zhang Xin.

185
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,320
- Don't come near me.
- Drop it.

186
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,640
Calm down.

187
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,440
Don't do anything reckless.

188
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:43,120
Put the knife down now.

189
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,400
Leave this place.

190
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:45,720
I'll pretend nothing happened here.

191
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:47,520
I already called the police.

192
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,880
I love you so much.

193
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,760
Yet you go and love someone else.

194
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:12,760
Calm down. Put the knife down.

195
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:18,839
You know what? Let's talk. Okay?

196
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,160
Tell me.

197
00:17:22,319 --> 00:17:23,359
What did I do wrong?

198
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,640
I think you need treatment.

199
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:29,680
I'll go with you to see a therapist.

200
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:30,800
No.

201
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,400
You used to call me a control freak.

202
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:36,080
You think I'm sick, don't you?

203
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:38,200
- You think I'm crazy?
- No, I do not.

204
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:40,800
But you cannot
let this obsession continue.

205
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,080
Give me the knife.

206
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,360
- Are you okay, Luan Nian?
- Are you out of your mind?

207
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:46,920
‪Luan Nian…

208
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:49,720
I'm fine.

209
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:51,960
- I…
- Again?

210
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,400
Are you okay?

211
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,040
Stop her.

212
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:24,080
Ms. Shang.

213
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:26,760
- You must have been terrified.
- No.

214
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,920
Please don't misunderstand.

215
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:32,840
They only dated briefly,

216
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,360
and they broke up a long time ago.

217
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:35,960
I can reassure you

218
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:38,720
that Luke would never two-time anyone.

219
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:40,080
No, you have the wrong idea.

220
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,840
We really are just colleagues.

221
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,240
He's my superior.

222
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:48,040
Then, you're the first co-worker
he brought to my restaurant.

223
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:54,400
That's because he has helped me a lot.

224
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,120
I wanted to buy him a meal to thank him.

225
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:02,360
Perhaps you didn't know
that Luke and I were co-workers once too.

226
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:06,240
In one year, I closed deals
worth 80 million yuan.

227
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:07,840
Yet he never bought me dinner.

228
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:11,400
Did you use to work in Lime too?

229
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,400
No.

230
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,400
Luke and I worked together
before he went to Lime.

231
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:17,880
He used to own
his own advertising company.

232
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:19,000
I worked under him.

233
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,640
Why did you two quit then?

234
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,360
We lost the drive.

235
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,360
In all those years,

236
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,880
we encountered many unreasonable clients.

237
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,560
Every day, our work could not be finished.

238
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,840
People couldn't be reasoned with.

239
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,040
They blew hot and cold.

240
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:40,120
And we spent every day carrying out
useless communication.

241
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,920
I quit. I was tired.

242
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:47,320
Why didn't he continue then?

243
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:50,440
Do not ever mention
his company before him.

244
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:51,600
He'll scowl at you.

245
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:55,280
We were betrayed by one of our own.

246
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,440
Luke was seriously affected by it.

247
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:01,120
Besides, his family prohibited him
from starting his own business.

248
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,760
What were you guys talking about?

249
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:06,200
How's your hand?

250
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:07,240
I'm fine.

251
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:09,160
The doctor said not to wet the wound.

252
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:10,080
Be mindful of that.

253
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:13,400
I'll leave you two be then.

254
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,440
I'll bring the car over.

255
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:21,720
Come. We'll drive you home.

256
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:23,640
I already hailed a taxi.

257
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,400
You two are leaving now?

258
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:26,360
Are you not going to look after her?

259
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,000
Why should I?

260
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,240
I already informed her family.

261
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:37,080
You must think
I'm an irresponsible playboy.

262
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,560
No.

263
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:42,800
Relationships can be messy
and complicated.

264
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:44,720
Worry not.

265
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,840
I won't tell anyone. I swear.

266
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:50,280
I do not believe in vows.

267
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,920
And I don't care about others' opinions.

268
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,040
She and I already broke up.

269
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:56,800
When two people first get together,

270
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:58,480
I think they often share the same goal.

271
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,520
But as time goes by,
people might change their minds.

272
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:03,880
It's no one's fault
if the relationship falls apart.

273
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:04,920
People want different things, that's all.

274
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,680
She chose to hold onto it,
and you chose to let go.

275
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:08,640
There's no right or wrong.

276
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:10,880
So you're saying
I should keep entangling with her,

277
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:12,520
even though I no longer love her.

278
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,160
No, I didn't say that.

279
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:20,400
I just think that love shouldn't
make one this miserable.

280
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,040
How many relationships have you had?

281
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,920
Just one.

282
00:21:28,520 --> 00:21:29,520
How was the breakup?

283
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,760
A reluctant separation
with mutual blessings?

284
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:36,560
We had good intentions
when we got together,

285
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:39,640
and we didn't break up unhappily.

286
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:44,400
You're quite mature when it comes to love.

287
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,120
I… I think my taxi is here.

288
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,240
Let me check.

289
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:26,000
Tao.

290
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,240
How come you're back?

291
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:29,920
Want to hang out tonight?

292
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,080
I can't.

293
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:33,080
I need to brush up on my English.

294
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,400
My colleagues all studied abroad.

295
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:35,720
I don't want to fall too far behind.

296
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:39,240
- You go ahead.
- You stay at home all the time.

297
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:41,400
You've been studying every day
during your days off.

298
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:43,640
You're affecting my after-work life.

299
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:45,000
All of you are here.

300
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:47,440
You should go out and relax.

301
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:48,360
It's Friday today.

302
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:51,120
I'm dumb, so I have to work harder.

303
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:55,040
Oh. My friends invited me to play the game
Legends of the Three Kingdoms later.

304
00:22:55,120 --> 00:22:56,080
Do you want to join us?

305
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,480
What did I just say?

306
00:22:58,560 --> 00:23:00,160
Friday is meant for fun.

307
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:02,000
LTK or the bar.

308
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:03,160
Pick one.

309
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:04,480
Neither.

310
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:10,080
Talk some sense into her.

311
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:15,640
Oh. I fixed this one. Take this.

312
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:22,600
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

313
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:28,920
Stop hesitating, Tao.

314
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,480
Sun's friends must be very smart.

315
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:33,400
Let's go meet some quality people.

316
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,920
It's just studying
in a different place, right?

317
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:36,720
So that's a deal then. I'll get changed.

318
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:37,800
Hurry up.

319
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:38,960
I changed my mind. I'll wear this.

320
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:40,040
It's pretty.

321
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:55,240
- Let me check on my cards.
- That's rough, buddy.

322
00:23:55,320 --> 00:23:56,880
Wait, how does "Kill" work?

323
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:58,080
- Can I just use "Dodge" to get out of it?
- Hello!

324
00:23:58,160 --> 00:24:00,080
- It's rare that Sun is willing to come out
- Hello.

325
00:24:00,160 --> 00:24:01,360
and he brought
two beautiful girls with him.

326
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:03,680
Introduce them to us.

327
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:07,280
I am Sun Yu.
You can call me Yu or Dabaoyu.

328
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:08,880
Hello.

329
00:24:08,960 --> 00:24:09,920
This is Tao.

330
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,120
- Shang Zhitao.
- Hello.

331
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:12,880
- Take a seat.
- Come.

332
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,840
- The drinks are here.
- Careful.

333
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:18,960
- Thanks.
- Hello.

334
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:21,120
My name is Long Zhentian.

335
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,480
Your Chinese is so good.

336
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:24,960
I am Feng Qiuhuang.

337
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:28,360
- Shang Zhitao.
- Hi.

338
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:31,200
Zhentian is my batchmate
from the university. He's Canadian.

339
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:33,240
His native languages
are English and French,

340
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:34,800
and he speaks really good Chinese.

341
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:36,840
I can tell.

342
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:39,120
You like playing LTK as a foreigner?

343
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:41,440
So-so. The third best player in the world.

344
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:49,840
I'm actually looking for a Chinese tutor
to practice my speaking skills.

345
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:51,160
You're looking for a Chinese tutor?

346
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:55,080
What a coincidence.
Tao is looking for an English tutor.

347
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:58,160
You two can exchange numbers
and study with one another.

348
00:24:58,240 --> 00:25:00,720
Wonderful. Give me a call.

349
00:25:01,320 --> 00:25:02,160
Type your number.

350
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:05,920
What's your goal
for your English proficiency?

351
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:09,480
As good as your Chinese proficiency.

352
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:12,200
Then, you'll have to work hard.

353
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:14,200
You too.

354
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:15,800
All right. Enough serious talk.

355
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:17,320
- Deal the cards now.
- Deal the cards.

356
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,080
Here. Take this.

357
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:34,000
Come in.

358
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:37,640
Boss. I'm leaving now.

359
00:25:43,240 --> 00:25:45,040
It's Friday today.

360
00:25:45,120 --> 00:25:46,880
You don't live to work.

361
00:25:48,440 --> 00:25:49,640
It's only 7 p.m.

362
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:51,200
But it's the weekend now.

363
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:53,680
A normal person would already
be queuing at a hot pot restaurant.

364
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:55,000
Just go.

365
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:56,400
Happy weekend.

366
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:58,200
Do go home early.

367
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:17,800
It seems Yuanzhu has been charmed.

368
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:19,680
- Allow me.
- Mince your words now.

369
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:21,600
- Thanks.
- If Sun gets mad,

370
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:23,120
he'll kill your character off.

371
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:25,680
Sun has a good temper. He won't kill you.

372
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:27,440
You don't know this.

373
00:26:27,520 --> 00:26:29,520
Back then, our boss stole his code

374
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,080
and even tried to pin
the blame on him and fire him.

375
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:33,800
And he just flipped the table.

376
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:35,560
I didn't know
you could be this aggressive.

377
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:37,480
You're always so even-tempered.

378
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:40,040
That guy must have been very awful
to make you this angry.

379
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:43,120
Guess what happened next?

380
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:47,000
That jerk couldn't understand
the logic behind Zhu's code.

381
00:26:47,080 --> 00:26:49,680
There was a bug, and he couldn't fix it.

382
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:53,320
So he came crawling back
and begged Zhu to come back.

383
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:55,560
You should've seen the face of that loser.

384
00:26:55,640 --> 00:27:00,680
Well, Zhu, what did you tell him?

385
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:06,760
I told him that at work,
nothing was a given.

386
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:08,320
No one should think that
they are above everyone else.

387
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:11,960
Without the effort of the employees,

388
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:13,600
no matter how big the company is,

389
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:15,760
it's just an empty shell.

390
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:17,080
Don't lie.

391
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:19,720
What you wanted to say was…

392
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:24,920
Screw you!

393
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:31,120
Come. Carry on.

394
00:27:31,200 --> 00:27:32,040
- Come.
- It's your turn now.

395
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:33,680
I use Invasion of Nanman.

396
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:42,400
- I don't have any strike cards.
- Strike cards.

397
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:43,520
I don't have any strike cards.

398
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,800
I still have one, Tao.

399
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:48,000
Sun Yu. They are having an event here.

400
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:49,360
Where are you?

401
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:51,120
Come now. Quick.

402
00:27:51,840 --> 00:27:54,520
Okay. Sure. I'll be there.

403
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:55,920
Okay.

404
00:27:58,600 --> 00:27:59,440
Sorry, guys.

405
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:03,000
My boss told me
something happened at the event.

406
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:04,960
I need to head back to fix it.

407
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:07,160
I have to go now.
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.

408
00:28:07,240 --> 00:28:09,200
My company can't live without me.

409
00:28:09,280 --> 00:28:10,720
I have to go now.

410
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,200
- Bye.
- Take care.

411
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:14,240
It's hard to get a ride here.
I'll drive you out.

412
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:16,200
- Okay.
- Let's go.

413
00:28:16,280 --> 00:28:17,160
Come.

414
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:19,200
It's getting late.
Let's head back as well.

415
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:20,480
- Okay.
- Okay.

416
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:21,560
We'll hang out another time.

417
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:23,040
- See you.
- Bye.

418
00:28:23,120 --> 00:28:24,640
- Bye.
- We'll go as well.

419
00:28:24,720 --> 00:28:26,160
- Bye.
- Bye.

420
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:32,560
Are you free later?

421
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:33,560
Do you have time?

422
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:36,000
Maybe we can have our first session today?

423
00:28:37,040 --> 00:28:38,160
Really?

424
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:39,120
Yes.

425
00:28:39,720 --> 00:28:41,320
Should we go somewhere else?

426
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,320
- Sure.
- Okay.

427
00:28:43,840 --> 00:28:44,800
Let me pack this up.

428
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:52,920
‪Hello.

429
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:54,200
Where are you?

430
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:55,360
About to drive home.

431
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:57,200
Song Qiuhan and Chen Kuannian are back.

432
00:28:57,280 --> 00:28:58,520
Let's grab a drink today.

433
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:00,000
- Their bar is launching today.
- No, thanks.

434
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:02,400
Dude. It's the weekend.

435
00:29:02,480 --> 00:29:05,160
Are you really going to stay at home
and talk to your fish?

436
00:29:05,840 --> 00:29:07,480
That's my time with my pet.

437
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:09,120
Fine.

438
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:12,280
If I cannot convince you,
the others will call you anyway.

439
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:13,800
Find a way to turn them down then.

440
00:29:13,880 --> 00:29:14,920
Hanging up.

441
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:34,560
This is the place.

442
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:35,720
It's new.

443
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:39,080
I heard there's
a special performance tonight.

444
00:29:39,160 --> 00:29:40,680
It's crowded.

445
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:44,080
Drifters in Beijing all gather here.

446
00:29:44,160 --> 00:29:45,760
It's the culture.

447
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:46,880
The culture.

448
00:29:57,960 --> 00:30:00,520
This is the soul of Beijing.

449
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:01,800
You work during the day.

450
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:04,160
You live at night.

451
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:05,480
It is quite different.

452
00:30:05,560 --> 00:30:07,440
When I first came to Beijing,

453
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:09,600
I could not speak a word of Chinese.

454
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:12,840
I learned it all from friends
I made in bars.

455
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:14,520
It's the same with English.

456
00:30:14,600 --> 00:30:16,120
You can't rely on textbooks alone.

457
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,680
You must come here

458
00:30:17,760 --> 00:30:21,080
and be immersed
in a real language environment.

459
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:23,640
Let me teach you how to order a drink.

460
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:30,920
Qiuhan.

461
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:32,640
How much did you invest in this place?

462
00:30:34,680 --> 00:30:36,200
- How much?
- Chen Kuannian invested in it as well.

463
00:30:36,280 --> 00:30:37,520
- We're in it together.
- What do you think?

464
00:30:38,600 --> 00:30:39,480
I invested in it too.

465
00:30:40,760 --> 00:30:42,440
You two sure are rich.

466
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:44,120
It is good.

467
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:45,200
This place is not bad, right?

468
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:46,920
- But your decor is…
- Decor is…

469
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:48,600
The location is good.

470
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:06,880
Is that you, Mr. Luan?

471
00:31:06,960 --> 00:31:08,200
Your fish finally let you out?

472
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:10,320
Luan Nian?

473
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:12,280
Let him out?

474
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:14,160
I bet his fish is sick of him,

475
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:15,800
so it kicked him out.

476
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:19,160
Since you're here,
then we must have a drink.

477
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:20,360
It's on you.

478
00:31:20,440 --> 00:31:21,480
Consider it your gift for my opening day.

479
00:31:21,560 --> 00:31:23,480
Don't. I just paid it.

480
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:25,000
As you should.

481
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:26,200
- Come.
- Come.

482
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:30,480
Hello.

483
00:31:43,680 --> 00:31:45,160
You need to work on your pronunciation.

484
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:55,040
Yes.

485
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:06,640
You said two martinis ten times.

486
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:07,640
That's 20 martinis.

487
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:20,800
Long Zhentian. We'll split the bill.

488
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:23,560
Okay.

489
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:25,880
Then, I'll teach you more things today.

490
00:32:25,960 --> 00:32:26,800
What do you want to learn?

491
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:31,760
I want to learn how to politely
turn down drinks during a business dinner.

492
00:32:32,760 --> 00:32:33,680
But…

493
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:35,400
You're Chinese,

494
00:32:35,480 --> 00:32:36,360
and you work in advertising.

495
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:38,520
How are you supposed
to close deals without drinking?

496
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:40,760
Even you say so.

497
00:32:40,840 --> 00:32:44,000
So, how do I learn to hold my drinks?

498
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:45,360
Just drink more.

499
00:32:45,440 --> 00:32:46,760
- Really?
- Yes.

500
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:58,280
Maybe recite some Chinese poems or idioms.

501
00:32:58,360 --> 00:32:59,560
It'll be even better.

502
00:32:59,640 --> 00:33:01,840
Quick. Teach me something.

503
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:05,720
What makes you drunk
is not liquor, but desires.

504
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:08,880
What makes you drunk
is not liquor, but desires.

505
00:33:08,960 --> 00:33:12,240
But sorrows feel even more bitter
when you drown them with liquor.

506
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:16,520
But sorrows feel even more bitter
when you drown them with liquor.

507
00:33:16,600 --> 00:33:18,320
Yes. Cheers.

508
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:19,360
Cheers.

509
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:29,640
Luke. We haven't heard you sing in years.

510
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:31,000
It's our opening day today.

511
00:33:31,080 --> 00:33:32,480
Sing for us.

512
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:33,640
No way.

513
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:35,520
Don't say no.

514
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:37,000
Everyone is here.

515
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:37,920
It's our bar.

516
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:39,160
You won't embarrass yourself.

517
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:41,520
No.

518
00:33:41,600 --> 00:33:43,800
You're still the same
as when you were at school.

519
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:44,720
You don't play along.

520
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:50,080
Just get off your pedestal
and let us enjoy your talent.

521
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:07,760
Will I get paid?

522
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:09,639
- I…
- Yes.

523
00:34:10,280 --> 00:34:11,719
When we were studying…

524
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:12,960
- How much was it again?
- 500 yuan.

525
00:34:13,040 --> 00:34:13,880
- Yes, 500 yuan.
- Yes, 500 yuan.

526
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:15,560
I'll pay you ten times that amount. No.

527
00:34:15,639 --> 00:34:20,199
If you can sing until morning,
I'll give this bar to you.

528
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:22,960
You might as well earn it.

529
00:34:29,360 --> 00:34:31,199
- Seriously?
- Here he goes.

530
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:32,199
He's doing it.

531
00:34:32,719 --> 00:34:33,800
Gosh!

532
00:34:36,719 --> 00:34:37,960
Yes!

533
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:54,320
Do you think Luan Nian
is quite distracted today?

534
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:55,679
What is he looking at?

535
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,120
Impossible.

536
00:34:57,200 --> 00:35:00,120
Who is this beauty who earns his gaze?

537
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:03,680
I think I know that girl.

538
00:35:03,760 --> 00:35:05,280
- Which one?
- Which one?

539
00:35:06,160 --> 00:35:07,480
Did he find a new girlfriend?

540
00:35:07,560 --> 00:35:08,640
No way.

541
00:35:08,720 --> 00:35:10,000
Why didn't he tell us?

542
00:35:15,840 --> 00:35:18,160
Anyway, I have to use the toilet.

543
00:37:22,160 --> 00:37:23,080
Luan Nian!

544
00:37:32,680 --> 00:37:33,520
Luan Nian?

545
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:39,200
Are you okay?

546
00:37:47,760 --> 00:37:49,520
- Where did he go?
- Who?

547
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:51,960
The singer.

548
00:37:52,040 --> 00:37:53,360
Luke.

549
00:37:54,640 --> 00:37:55,640
Sorry, but…

550
00:37:55,720 --> 00:37:58,120
No one was singing.

551
00:37:58,200 --> 00:37:59,760
Are you drunk?

552
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:01,640
Can you continue?

553
00:38:03,680 --> 00:38:04,640
A toast to music.

554
00:38:04,720 --> 00:38:06,040
A toast to friends.

555
00:38:06,720 --> 00:38:07,680
A toast to good food.

556
00:38:07,760 --> 00:38:09,320
A toast to stupid people.

557
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:26,240
I can't drink anymore.

558
00:38:26,320 --> 00:38:28,600
I want to go home.

559
00:38:31,280 --> 00:38:33,280
- Not bad, Luan Nian.
- You still have it.

560
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:34,760
Pay up.

561
00:38:34,840 --> 00:38:36,440
Foot the bill now.

562
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:39,360
I asked you to sing until morning,
not just one song.

563
00:38:39,440 --> 00:38:41,640
Thank you.

564
00:38:49,000 --> 00:38:50,080
Hey, hey.

565
00:38:50,160 --> 00:38:51,800
Hey, calm down. Calm down.

566
00:38:51,880 --> 00:38:52,840
What's happening?

567
00:38:55,320 --> 00:38:56,400
What are you doing?

568
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:58,040
- Easy now.
- What's going on?

569
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:01,120
- Girlfriend?
- Luke.

570
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:06,920
It's you.

571
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:29,200
Are you really her tutor?

572
00:39:29,280 --> 00:39:31,000
- Cheers.
- Yes.

573
00:39:31,080 --> 00:39:32,200
Private English tutor.

574
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:33,840
Let's go.

575
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:34,760
No.

576
00:39:39,080 --> 00:39:40,800
She hasn't finished her work.

577
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:43,840
It's the weekend.

578
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,280
What work?

579
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:51,280
Are you done with the summary report?

580
00:39:51,360 --> 00:39:52,640
And here you are, at a bar.

581
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:53,960
Summary report?

582
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:55,120
Not done yet.

583
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:56,600
Can you teach me?

584
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:57,800
Sure.

585
00:39:58,560 --> 00:39:59,560
I'll drive you home.

586
00:40:02,120 --> 00:40:03,240
Wow.

587
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:05,200
Easy now. Come.

588
00:40:05,280 --> 00:40:06,120
- They are working.
- I'll be going now.

589
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:06,880
- Come. Let's drink.
- Let's drink.

590
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:07,680
- Bye.
- Come. Let's drink.

591
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:08,920
Let's drink.

592
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:20,600
- Stand straight.
- Stand straight.

593
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:22,920
I'll buy some water to sober you up.

594
00:40:23,000 --> 00:40:25,040
I'll buy some water to sober you up.

595
00:40:25,120 --> 00:40:26,160
Stand straight!

596
00:40:28,560 --> 00:40:30,000
You're doing this on purpose, aren't you?

597
00:40:31,160 --> 00:40:33,520
How can you be this handsome

598
00:40:34,040 --> 00:40:35,360
when you're angry?

599
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:37,600
Stop it.

600
00:40:40,680 --> 00:40:41,520
What?

601
00:40:42,760 --> 00:40:44,680
They say you are very mean,

602
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:46,400
but I don't think so.

603
00:40:47,560 --> 00:40:50,280
You just have a duck bill.

604
00:40:51,640 --> 00:40:53,640
A duck bill. You know what?

605
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:56,600
A duck bill is like this.

606
00:40:58,600 --> 00:40:59,680
Useless Lumi.

607
00:41:00,200 --> 00:41:01,760
Look.

608
00:41:05,760 --> 00:41:06,800
Like this.

609
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:09,280
You keep appearing in my dreams.

610
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:10,560
Like this.

611
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:12,480
What happened in the dream?

612
00:41:14,280 --> 00:41:15,760
I…

613
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:18,600
I…

614
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:22,080
I was scolding you.

615
00:41:23,480 --> 00:41:26,280
You wish. Shang Zhitao.

616
00:41:27,560 --> 00:41:30,520
It's time for you to lose weight
because you're about to break my arms.

617
00:41:30,600 --> 00:41:31,800
Luan Nian!

618
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:35,280
My dad tells me to eat more.

619
00:41:35,360 --> 00:41:36,960
Otherwise, a strong gust of wind
will blow me away.

620
00:41:38,040 --> 00:41:39,200
Tell your father not to worry

621
00:41:39,280 --> 00:41:40,800
because you have aced that task.

622
00:41:49,520 --> 00:41:50,440
Is your dad good to you?

623
00:41:50,520 --> 00:41:51,560
Is your dad not good to you?

624
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:56,360
Does he know you're stupid?

625
00:41:57,240 --> 00:41:58,160
You're drinking
when your ankle is barely healed.

626
00:42:00,560 --> 00:42:02,160
Do not underestimate me.

627
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:04,960
I am slow,

628
00:42:05,480 --> 00:42:10,680
but every step I take is very real.

629
00:42:15,080 --> 00:42:16,400
See?

630
00:42:16,480 --> 00:42:18,520
- Did you see it?
- Yes.

631
00:42:19,160 --> 00:42:20,120
Let me show you.

632
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:27,720
Yes, very real. Come.

633
00:42:33,560 --> 00:42:35,200
Mister. To Tiantong Dongyuan.

634
00:42:35,280 --> 00:42:36,360
To Tiantongyuan.

635
00:42:45,800 --> 00:42:50,200
SHANG ZHITAO

636
00:42:56,320 --> 00:42:59,120
SUN YU

637
00:43:05,400 --> 00:43:08,760
TIANTONG DONGYUAN, SECTION 1

638
00:43:15,240 --> 00:43:16,600
Over there.

639
00:43:30,760 --> 00:43:31,800
Sixty what?

640
00:43:33,920 --> 00:43:34,960
6…

641
00:43:35,720 --> 00:43:37,920
602.

642
00:43:38,600 --> 00:43:39,720
Sunflower.

643
00:43:39,800 --> 00:43:41,640
The one with a sunflower.

644
00:43:48,720 --> 00:43:49,840
Sit down.

645
00:43:59,040 --> 00:44:00,440
I am not drunk.

646
00:44:02,680 --> 00:44:04,680
Who is it?

647
00:44:06,160 --> 00:44:07,480
Who are you?

648
00:44:09,520 --> 00:44:10,880
Crazy.

649
00:44:12,360 --> 00:44:13,560
Sun Yu.

650
00:44:15,080 --> 00:44:16,160
Sun Yu!

651
00:44:16,240 --> 00:44:18,920
Stop it, or I'll call the police.

652
00:44:28,640 --> 00:44:29,760
Where is your home?

653
00:44:31,800 --> 00:44:33,680
I don't know.

654
00:44:34,960 --> 00:44:36,480
I want to sleep.

655
00:44:42,400 --> 00:44:43,960
Does it still hurt?

656
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:46,440
No.

657
00:44:53,800 --> 00:44:56,080
I got this when I was saving you.

658
00:44:56,160 --> 00:44:58,800
Back in ancient times…

659
00:45:08,680 --> 00:45:10,040
You'd have to marry me.

660
00:45:31,120 --> 00:45:32,160
Come home with me.

661
00:46:03,960 --> 00:46:05,880
You're quite mature when it comes to love.

662
00:46:12,960 --> 00:46:16,400
You must think
I'm an irresponsible playboy.

663
00:46:19,080 --> 00:46:22,880
Isn't an amicable separation
what breaking up is all about?

664
00:46:54,560 --> 00:46:55,440
I knew it.

665
00:46:55,520 --> 00:46:59,640
When you relax,
your brain will betray you.

666
00:46:59,720 --> 00:47:03,040
Instead of finding ways
to gain a footing at work,

667
00:47:03,120 --> 00:47:05,280
I think of useless things like this.
